<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!-- The ONLY project shared between services, and it must stay that way.
       Message records and nothing else: no domain logic, no EF Core types, no behaviour,
       no base classes with methods on them.

       The reason is not tidiness. A shared library containing behaviour has to be
       versioned and released in lockstep by everyone who references it, which quietly
       turns a set of independently deployable services back into one deployable. A
       library of immutable records describing messages does not create that pressure,
       because adding an optional field to a record breaks nobody.

       Deliberately no package references. If one is ever needed here, that is a signal
       that something has crept in which does not belong. -->

</Project>
